description:
Edit repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/docs-align-tick.ts. This is ONE contiguous string replacement. The new code is fully wired on the live path — it adds no unreferenced symbol.

old_string (this exact 6-line block, which occurs exactly once in the file):
  const vocabulary = await deriveNamingVocabulary(documents);
  const scan = await resolveDocsAlignScan({
    type: "docs_align_scan",
    corpus: { documents },
    live_truth: { existing_paths, unit_names },
    invariants: ["timelessness", "naming_alignment", "setup_enablement"],

new_string:
  const vocabulary = await deriveNamingVocabulary(documents);
  let advertised_shapes: string[] = [];
  try {
    const base = (process.env["DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8100").replace(/\/+$/, "");
    const res = await fetch(`${base}/registry/shapes`, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000) });
    if (res.ok) {
      const j = (await res.json()) as unknown;
      const arr = Array.isArray(j)
        ? j
        : Array.isArray((j as { shapes?: unknown })?.shapes)
          ? (j as { shapes: unknown[] }).shapes
          : [];
      advertised_shapes = arr.filter((s): s is string => typeof s === "string");
    }
  } catch {
    advertised_shapes = [];
  }
  const scan = await resolveDocsAlignScan({
    type: "docs_align_scan",
    corpus: { documents },
    live_truth: { existing_paths, unit_names, advertised_shapes },
    invariants: ["timelessness", "naming_alignment", "setup_enablement", "accuracy"],

Everything after that block — the `vocabulary,` line, `max_findings: 100,` and the closing `});` — stays exactly as it is. Do not touch them.

WHY THIS IS ONE CHANGE AND NOT TWO: a previous attempt added a standalone `fetchAdvertisedShapes` helper and deliberately left the wiring for later. It was correctly rejected — "compose adds top-level function fetchAdvertisedShapes with zero readers, not exported and not wired — a write-only hollow addition; wire it, export it for a real consumer, or drop it". So the fetch is inlined here as a statement whose result is consumed on the very next lines. There is no new function declaration, nothing unexported, and nothing unreferenced.

WHAT IT FIXES: the `accuracy` invariant in docs-align-scan.ts has never once executed, for two independent reasons that this single edit closes together. (1) It was absent from the invariants array passed by this caller. (2) Its branch is gated at docs-align-scan.ts line 236 on `pointer.live_truth.advertised_shapes`, and this caller built live_truth as `{ existing_paths, unit_names }` only — both from the local filesystem, exactly as the comment above it says: "Assemble live_truth from local filesystem only". The tick never queried the discovery registry, so advertised_shapes was permanently undefined and the branch was skipped even when requested. accuracy is the only invariant that compares a document against live truth; the other three check style, vocabulary and file existence.

SAFETY: every failure path leaves advertised_shapes as an empty array — non-ok response, JSON parse failure, unreachable discovery, timeout. With an empty array the accuracy branch simply finds nothing, which is exactly today's behaviour. The change can improve the result or no-op; it cannot throw. No import is needed: process.env, fetch and AbortSignal are globals. The `.replace(/\/+$/, "")` endpoint normalisation matches the idiom already used in orphaned-capability-scan.ts and residual-shape-discovery.ts.

Do NOT modify walkMd, walkScripts, deriveNamingVocabulary, or any other function in this file.

